DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iiccoonnvvlliisstt() function obtains a list of character encodings that are
     supported by the iconv(3) call.  The ddoo__oonnee() callback function will be
     called, where the _c_o_u_n_t argument will be set to the number of the encod‐
     ing names found, the _n_a_m_e_s argument will be the list of the supported en‐
     coding names and the _a_r_g argument will be the _a_r_g argument of the
     iiccoonnvvlliisstt() function.  This argument can be used to interchange custom
     data between the caller of iiccoonnvvlliisstt() and the callback function.

     If an error occurs, _n_a_m_e_s will be NULL when calling ddoo__oonnee().

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     __iconv_free_list(3), __iconv_get_list(3), iconv(3)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The iiccoonnvvlliisstt function is a non-standard extension, which appeared in the
     GNU implementation and was adopted in FreeBSD 9.0 for compatibility's
     sake.

